  "description": "GIDRER crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C86 H90 Ho4 Mn6 N8 O48,5(C1 H4 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Ho1B (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2B (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1B (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn2B (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3B (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.553-3.971 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.36-123.74°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ho4Mn6(H2shi)2(shi)6(sal)2(O2CCH3)4(OH)2(CH3OH)8]·4CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
